# STATIC BOOT DEFAULT for Liquidsoap. Concrete counterpart to icecast.default.xml
# with the SAME dev source password, so Liquidsoap can connect to Icecast on a
# cold start before the app has rendered config from the DB.
#
# The container seeds this onto the shared streamconfig volume only if no
# radio.env exists yet. The app overwrites radio.env with real DB values once it
# boots, and config-watch.sh restarts the container onto them within seconds. Do
# NOT put real secrets here — this file is committed.
ICECAST_HOST='icecast'
ICECAST_PORT='8000'
ICECAST_SOURCE_PASSWORD='devsource'
STREAM_MOUNT='/live.mp3'
STREAM_BITRATE='128'
# The optional format mounts, all off. An EMPTY PATH is how off is spelled: radio.liq
# builds an encoder and an output only for a format whose mount it was given a name
# for, so a station that never asked for these pays nothing for them. The app fills
# these in from stream.opusEnabled / stream.aacEnabled / stream.flacEnabled and derives
# the paths from STREAM_MOUNT by swapping the extension.
#
# The bitrates are a closed set, matching the branch in radio.liq and the menu the
# console offers: the encoders take this figure when the script is PARSED and cannot be
# handed one later, so a free-typed number would be a figure the stream cannot honour.
# FLAC has no bitrate; it is lossless.
STREAM_MOUNT_OPUS=''
STREAM_OPUS_BITRATE=''
STREAM_MOUNT_AAC=''
STREAM_AAC_BITRATE=''
STREAM_MOUNT_FLAC=''
STREAM_FLAC_BITRATE=''
# The HLS output, off. An empty directory is how off is spelled, on the same rule as an
# empty mount path: a writer with nowhere to write is not a writer. When the app renders
# a real value it is the path INSIDE this container, which is not the one the app reads
# its playlists back from -- both see one volume at their own mount points.
STREAM_HLS_DIR=''
STREAM_HLS_SEGMENT_SECONDS='2'
STREAM_HLS_SEGMENT_COUNT='6'
STREAM_NAME='Deadair'
STREAM_DESCRIPTION=''
STREAM_GENRE='Music'
STREAM_URL=''
# BCP 47 tag sent as Content-Language on the source connection. Empty sends no header.
STREAM_LANGUAGE=''
MUSIC_DIR='/music'
# Harbor voice input the app pushes rendered DJ audio to (see radio.liq step 3).
# HARBOR_PORT must match the port published in docker-compose.yml. HARBOR_PASSWORD
# is a dev default only — the app overwrites radio.env with a strong secret from the
# DB, which the container adopts on the restart config-watch.sh triggers. Do NOT put a
# real secret here.
HARBOR_PORT='8005'
HARBOR_PASSWORD='devharbor'
# Playout wiring: where Liquidsoap reports the item that actually started (an item is pushed,
# and downloaded, one item ahead of air), and the shared secret gating that call plus the app's
# pushes to /control/*. There is no pull URL: the app pushes the rundown in. The app-rendered
# radio.env fills these from the DB; an empty secret here means the control endpoints reject
# everything, so the serve-mode bed stays inactive until the app is configured.
PLAYOUT_AIRED_URL=''
# The other push back to the app: the running order stopped producing while the lease was held (the
# mount has fallen through to the local bed), and it started again. Empty means do not report, so a
# stream pointed at an app without the route falls back to that app's own two-second reconcile.
PLAYOUT_STARVE_URL=''
PLAYOUT_BRIDGE_SECRET=''
# The dead-man switch: how long one "deadair is driving" assertion holds the mount, in seconds.
# Nothing airs unless the app renews it inside this window, so a crashed or restarted app takes
# the station off air rather than leaving the local bed playing to nobody's plan. Must comfortably
# exceed the app's 2s reconcile interval; the app materializes its own value over this one.
CONTROL_TTL_S='6'
# How many requests Liquidsoap DOWNLOADS ahead of the one on air. This is what makes a skip land at
# once: only this many pushed items are ever resolved, so with the Liquidsoap default of 1 a second
# skip during the replacement's download has nothing fetched to cut to and is swallowed. The app
# materializes this from the same constant it uses for its own push lead.
PLAYOUT_PREFETCH='3'
# The duck (talk-over mode): how far the music bed drops under the DJ voice and how long the
# ramp takes. Director settings duckGainDb / duckFadeMs; these are only the cold-start defaults.
DUCK_GAIN_DB='-12'
DUCK_FADE_MS='300'
# The operator's trim on the DJ voice, in dB, applied after the mic chain and on top of the gain the
# app stamps on each segment (`liq_amplify`, from that segment's level against playout.targetLufs).
# Zero because the app now decides the level: this is the last word for an operator who wants the DJ
# a decibel forward of where that lands, not the per-engine correction it used to have to be.
VOICE_GAIN_DB='0'
# Deliberately absent here: CONFIG_STAMP, a short hash the app writes over the content of the
# radio.env it renders. radio.liq reports it on every /control/* reading, and the app compares it
# against the file as it stands to see whether this process is still running the config that was
# rendered for it — the whole point being that nothing re-reads this file after the entrypoint
# sources it, so a re-render leaves a live container holding replaced secrets with no symptom that
# names the cause. A container booted on THIS file has no stamp, which the app reads as "cannot
# say" rather than as a mismatch. See apps/api/src/modules/stream/stream.staleness.ts.
